# Prog 3: a Scrubbly (9x9 pixels), left column A, top row C.
# It is left-right symmetric, so only columns 0-4 are stored (three per
# number) and the renderer mirrors them: E = 2A+8 puts the mirror
# axis on the centre column. W=3 and H=9 are already set by the ladders.
2A+8→E:90786392→D:Prog 4:124290522→D:Prog 4
